1
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:09,429
The insurer has given the denial to a
machine, and the machine answers in
seconds.

2
00:00:09,429 --> 00:00:20,143
The physician has been given nothing,
and must meet in hours what was done in
an instant, so most denials are never
met at all.

3
00:00:20,143 --> 00:00:27,000
Everything shown was built this week, on
my pre-existing record system, appeal
engine, and coverage index.

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:34,286
I asked whether Meta's models, one of
them open weights, could prepare that
reply from the chart,

5
00:00:34,286 --> 00:00:42,857
with every sentence held to the record
by a deterministic check, and decline
when the record could not support one.

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,429
Fifty synthetic denials, no real patient
anywhere; thirty the chart can answer,
twenty it cannot.

7
00:00:49,429 --> 00:00:56,714
Left to right: the physician's record,
the payer's rules under the payer's own
reason, and the appeal.

8
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:57,429
Play.

9
00:00:57,429 --> 00:01:07,286
Spark 1.3 first asks my coverage index
when this payer's criteria last changed,
then opens only the entries it needs,
eleven of twenty-six.

10
00:01:07,286 --> 00:01:10,714
Every sentence cites one entry and
quotes it.

11
00:01:10,714 --> 00:01:21,000
A deterministic gate, not a model,
checks that the quote is in that entry
and that every number, date, code, and
side is sourced.

12
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:22,286
Eight of eight.

13
00:01:22,286 --> 00:01:22,714
Pass.

14
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:31,143
Test the gate yourself: change one
number in a verified sentence and it
refutes the edit, in the browser.

15
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:42,286
Live, not a replay: Spark 1.3 reads the
chart, says why it opens each entry, and
ends on the record hash the page shows.

16
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:52,857
A case the chart cannot answer: Muse
Wonder read all twenty-two entries
looking for the sepsis criterion, found
nothing, and declined, naming it.

17
00:01:52,857 --> 00:01:57,143
Declining is the right answer for twenty
of the fifty.

18
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:06,571
The scoreboard: nine kept runs;
agreement with the key, forty-five to
fifty of fifty; no fabricated quote in
any sentence;

19
00:02:06,571 --> 00:02:09,571
Spark 1.3 under a dollar a run.

20
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,714
Compare: three models, one case, side by
side, every sentence stamped.

21
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:29,143
Back to the pass, and the writ: the
draft as the instrument the physician
would sign, every sentence footnoted to
the entry it quotes, the plan's own
reason answered, the signature line
blank.

22
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,143
Print it or save it as text; nothing
leaves this page signed.

23
00:02:35,143 --> 00:02:42,429
The gate verifies that a statement is in
the record, not that the record
satisfies the criterion.

24
00:02:42,429 --> 00:02:46,286
The machine prepares the instrument and
cannot issue it.

25
00:02:46,286 --> 00:02:50,571
The physician's signature is what makes
the draft a writ.
